# Supplied menu soundtrack - 2026-11-01

The player and vector covers described below were superseded later the same day by `MUSIC_PLAYER_REDESIGN_2026_11_01.md`.

The fourteen complete mixes supplied in `temp/audio` replace Exploration for menu and results playback. Each is copied byte-for-byte into `game/assets/audio/soundtrack_2026_v1/`; the source files remain in place. The catalogue provides fourteen original vector travel-poster sleeves, and the record player supports browsing, selecting, previous/next, pause and volume. Tracks advance in supplied order and wrap; automatic changes update the current profile's in-memory selection even after another save replaces its settings dictionary. Existing old catalogue selections migrate to the first track. Race/practice music remains disabled.

The manifest alongside the audio records source and installed SHA-256 hashes, the owner's requested use and the unknown provenance/licence. The user did not supply creator, generator, or distribution terms; these remain unverified. No music was edited, generated or subjectively auditioned. The old files remain for historical provenance and are no longer selected by the menu.

Validation used the pinned Godot 4.7.2 engine with isolated test user directories and the scoped crash-dialog wrapper. `test_supplied_soundtrack.gd` passed 41 headless and 43 desktop Compatibility checks, including all fourteen imported MP3 streams and distinct mipmapped covers, legacy migration, selection/skip, settings replacement, native end-of-track signal and nonzero Music-bus output with the dummy driver. `test_biome_music_off.gd` passed 42 headless checks. Desktop `app.gd` and `game.gd` checks were run separately. The sandbox reported a root certificate-store read error during tests; these checks did not use network access. Some runs reported shutdown resource leaks; a later native run exited without them. Owner listening, visual review in the actual Garage, physical-device playback, and distribution licensing remain open.
